WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.939
Oberyn Martell: "Unbowed, Unbent, Unbroken."

00:00:03.939 --> 00:00:11.219
The words of House Martell.A promise to our
enemies and a challenge to our lovers.

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:15.610
Thousands of years ago, the warrior queen
Nymeria crossed into Dorne from Essos, fleeing

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.180
the dragonlords of Valyria.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.790
After she landed, she burned her ships, all
ten thousand of them, so no cowards could

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.170
slink home.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.670
What a woman.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.980
Dornish in spirit before she ever was in flesh.

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.760
She was lucky to land in Dorne, where powerful
women are not locked away in septs and the

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.000
beds of old men.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.140
My ancestor, Mors Martell, saw her and desired
her, and proved that where armies fail, a

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.239
tongue may succeed.

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:55.329
Wedding his strength to hers, his spear to
her sun, they subdued all of his rivals together.

00:00:55.329 --> 00:01:01.190
After the tradition of her people, House Martell
then ruled Dorne as Princes, not kings, unless

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.270
the eldest child was a daughter.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:27.650
For unlike the rest 

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:37.290
of Westeros, we follow a Prince or a Princess
Martell just the same, and we always have.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:43.509
Some people forget that Aegon Targaryen crowned
himself lord of six kingdoms, not seven.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:49.061
When his sister marched on Dorne, she found
no mighty hosts drawn up against her for her

00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:51.930
dragon to burn and her soldiers to slaughter.

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.329
The sands swirled, men died, and her dragon
saw nothing.

00:01:55.329 --> 00:02:01.909
The sun shone, men died, and her dragon bowed
to our greater fire.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:07.790
The Targaryens retreated with their tails
tucked between their legs.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:11.230
Of course, in later years, his descendants
would try again.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:17.790
Daeron the First succeeded at great cost and
reigned in Dorne for a few glorious months.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.020
One night, his steward pulled down a sash
by his bed to summon his consorts.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:27.580
Instead, the canopy split open, and a hundred
red scorpions fell on him.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.980
He was a Tyrell.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.840
You would think he would be used to getting
stung.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:37.920
Within a fortnight, House Martell again ruled
a free Dorne.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.150
Twice the Targaryens tried to conquer Dorne
with soldiers.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.520
Twice they failed.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.120
Only when the dragon kings came bearing husbands
and wives did my ancestors relent and agree

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.940
to join their Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:57.730
House Martell could have waged war until the
end of days, but how could we resist a peace

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:00.130
we could take to bed?

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:06.290
Eventually, after centuries of courtship,
House Martell got into bed with the Targaryens.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:11.599
We took King Daeron II and his sister for
our own before they could take each other,

00:03:11.599 --> 00:03:13.900
and six kingdoms became seven.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.450
Even now, I do not blame my ancestors.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.890
One look at those long silver locks.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.620
It is not every day a man gets to ride a dragon.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:29.540
Viserys Targaryen: After the submission of
House Stark, Aegon marches towards Oldtown,

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.569
steeling himself for another battle.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:37.270
But he found the gates open, with the High
Septon welcoming him.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:43.010
The pious fool even had the arrogance to grant
what Aegon had already won, and anointed the

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:49.769
last Valyrian as "Aegon of House Targaryen,
First of His Name, King of the Andals and

00:03:49.769 --> 00:03:55.390
the First Men, Lord of the Seven Kingdoms
and Protector of the Realm."

00:03:55.390 --> 00:04:01.920
Varys: But while Aegon titled himself Lord
of the Seven Kingdoms, in reality, he held

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.260
only six.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.120
The seventh, Dorne, had never knelt.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.920
Visenya had flown into the Vale and returned
with its crown.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:16.680
Mimicking her sister, Rhaenys had flown over
the enemy force holding the passes into Dorne

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:22.260
and landed in the castle of its ruling lady,
Princess Meria of House Martell.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:26.500
Meria was eighty years old, fat, bald, and
blind.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:31.509
Behind her back, many sniggered at her as
the "Yellow Toad of Dorne."

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:34.410
The beautiful Rhaenys probably thought as
much when they met.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:39.260
She demanded Princess Meria kneel to her brother
Aegon, though she allowed that on account

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:43.340
of Meria's age and health, a simple vow of
submission would do.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:49.260
But the princess told the queen that the Targaryens
weren't wanted in Dorne, and no Martell would

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.050
ever bow, bend or break no matter how badly
they burned.

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:58.460
Rhaenys could have mounted her dragon right
then, and roasted Meria in the castle as her

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:00.449
brother had done at Harrenhal.

00:05:00.449 --> 00:05:06.280
But whatever she saw in Meria's eyes scared
her right back to King's Landing, with a dragon's

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.140
tail between its legs.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:15.650
After Aegon's coronation, Rhaenys returned
to Dorne with Aegon and Visenya and their

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.650
dragons.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:21.479
But no armies met them in the field, and no
lords defied them in their castles.

00:05:21.479 --> 00:05:26.000
As the dragons approached, Dorne simply emptied.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.100
House Martell had learned from Harrenhal and
the Field of Fire.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:34.820
The dragons were unbeatable in battle, but
wars were more than battles.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.990
Unopposed, Aegon claimed Dorne for his own.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:43.070
But as soon as he returned to King's Landing,
his castellans were hurled off towers, and

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:47.290
his royal garrison vanished in the desert,
never to be seen again.

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:54.410
Except, perhaps, when the winds change and
the sands cough up old bones and armor.Rhaenys

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:59.820
returned on Meraxes, intent on avenging herself
against Meria Martell.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.210
But Dorne was no longer empty.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:08.229
The Dornish kept Meria's promise and fought
even while burning under dragon flame.

00:06:08.229 --> 00:06:10.790
And they won.

00:06:10.790 --> 00:06:15.930
One day a bolt pierced the eye of Meraxes
and knocked the dragon out of the sky.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.520
House Martell remained unbroken, unlike the
unfortunate Rhaenys.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:27.350
In their wrath, Aegon and Visenya set flame
to every castle and city but Sunspear, trying

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.580
to turn the people against House Martell.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:35.759
But the Dornish stayed loyal, and when Aegon
returned to King's Landing, he found assassins

00:06:35.759 --> 00:06:38.740
waiting for him in the streets of his own
capital.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:44.009
If not for Visenya, the Conqueror would not
have enjoyed his conquest for very long.

00:06:44.009 --> 00:06:48.710
From then on, the king and his family would
be guarded by the seven greatest knights in

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:52.160
the realm: the Kingsguard.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:56.910
When Meria died in her sleep, a weak and tired
son sued for peace.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:02.919
But old Meria had exhausted Aegon as well,
and he granted the request.

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:07.410
The Targaryens still wanted Dorne, and eventually,
they would have it, but not at the point of

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:08.559
a sword.

00:07:08.559 --> 00:07:13.710
They would buy it the same way great lords
buy anything: with a daughter.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:20.710
Ellaria Sand: Before the Seven Kingdoms, before
the Iron Throne, there was Dorne.

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:26.940
Twelve thousand years ago, the First Men crossed
the land bridge from Essos to here.

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.560
Of course, they were men, so they soon broke
it.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:35.500
Then, while their cousins to the North built
kingdoms, the Dornish squabbled over land,

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:40.250
water, and wives for centuries.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.850
Until Nymeria, a warrior princess in Essos.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:49.210
She led a fleet of ten thousand ships across
the Narrow Sea to Dorne.

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:53.090
Almost all of the petty lords made it clear
that she wasn't welcome.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:55.830
All but one.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:58.870
Mors of House Martell.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:04.600
He saw in her a strength to match any man,
including his rivals.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:09.009
After she accepted his marriage offer, she
set fire to her ships.

00:08:09.009 --> 00:08:16.400
For fifty leagues, the coast was bright as
day, and in the burning light, Princess Nymeria

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:22.569
named Mors Martell the Prince of Dorne, in
the style of her people.

00:08:22.569 --> 00:08:27.889
Dorne would be her home or her grave.

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:32.820
For many years, Nymeria and Mors waged war
against all rivals.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:39.880
The Jordaynes, Blackmonts, Qorgyles, and even
the mighty House Yronwood.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:46.360
They sent no fewer than six self-styled "kings"
to the Wall in golden chains.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:53.700
After Mors fell in battle, Nymeria took command
of his armies and united Dorne in two years.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:58.270
She ruled for twenty-seven more, and though
she married again, those husbands were little

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:02.209
more than councilors and consorts.

00:09:02.209 --> 00:09:06.870
Dorne was Nymeria, and Nymeria was Dorne.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:12.010
She survived a dozen attempts on her life,
put down two rebellions, and threw back two

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.010
invasions.

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:19.540
And when at last, she died, her eldest child
succeeded her (her daughter, not her son),

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:25.279
and Dorne followed her because Nymeria had
proven that women were equal to men, if not

00:09:25.279 --> 00:09:26.550
better.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:33.190
Centuries later, Aegon Targaryen sought to
unite Westeros, as Nymeria had Dorne.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:37.420
The other six kingdoms fell quickly before
his dragons and ambition.

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:42.880
When his sister-wife, Rhaenys, flew her dragon
south and demanded Dorne's surrender as well,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:49.779
Princess Meria Martell warned, "I will not
fight you, nor will I kneel to you.

00:09:49.779 --> 00:09:51.380
Dorne has no king.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.980
Tell your brother that."

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.640
Rhaenys threatened that the next time the
Targaryens would come with fire and blood.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:10:06.230
Meria replied, "You may burn us, my lady,
but you will not bend us, break us or make

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.340
us bow.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:11.779
This is Dorne; you are not wanted here.

00:10:11.779 --> 00:10:13.649
Return at your peril!"

00:10:13.649 --> 00:10:17.910
Rhaenys did, and she died.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.100
Her dragon died.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:22.209
All her soldiers died.

00:10:22.209 --> 00:10:30.060
Eventually, her brother, the Conqueror, conceded
that what Nymeria had done, he could not undo.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:35.890
Generations later, another foolish Targaryen
invaded Dorne.

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:37.580
He died as well.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:43.779
Eventually, we did join the Seven Kingdoms,
but when we wanted and on our terms.

00:10:43.779 --> 00:10:49.459
If dragons could not conquer us, why should
we fear lions?

00:10:49.459 --> 00:10:52.790
"Unbowed, unbent, unbroken."

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:57.060
The words of House Martell.The words of Dorne.

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.220
Men may forget, but women always remember.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.370
When we were divided, Nymeria united us.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:22.860
When we were invaded, Meria defended us.

